Q. 8 What happens if I break rules?
Server Violations & Penalty Guidelines
Violation Categories & Consequences
Minor Violations
Examples:
Off-topic discussions in wrong channels
Minor spam or excessive messaging
First-time minor misconduct
Inappropriate use of bot commands

Penalties:
1st Offense: Verbal Warning
 2nd Offense: Official Warning (logged by Wick bot)
 3rd Offense: Temporary Mute (1-24 hours)
 Continued: Kick from server

Major Violations
Examples:
Harassment, hate speech, discrimination
Sharing NSFW or offensive content
Advertising, DM spam, or server invites
Repeated minor violations after warnings
Scamming or fraudulent activities

Penalties:
 1st Major Offense: Temporary Ban (3-7 days)
2nd Major Offense: Extended Ban (14-30 days)
 3rd Major Offense: Permanent Ban

Severe Violations
Examples:
Impersonation of staff or community members
Severe harassment, doxxing, or threats
Sharing malicious code, hacking, or illegal content
Ban evasion using alternate accounts
Any illegal activities or content

Penalties:
Immediate Permanent Ban
All associated accounts banned
Report to Discord Trust & Safety

Appeals Process
How to Appeal:
Wait few hours after penalty
Check your Wick dm for Appeals process
Provide context and acknowledge wrongdoing
Show understanding of rules

What Helps Your Appeal:
Genuine apology and accountability
Demonstrating rule understanding
Time passed showing reflection
Previous positive contribution history

Important Notes
 Context Matters: Staff consider intent, history, and circumstances
 Progressive Discipline: Penalties increase with repeat offenses
Zero Tolerance: Severe violations = immediate permanent ban
 Appeals: Not all bans are appealable, especially severe violations

Our Goal
We aim to maintain a safe, welcoming, and productive environment for all community members while being fair and consistent in our moderation approach.

Questions? Contact our moderation team! via Support Ticket Here
